       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum labeled dose. It gives no added glycemic benefit and carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. I can't find a clinical scenario where that dose would be appropriate.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose within the labeled range.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf 2550 mg was meant as the total daily dose, I'll enter the 850 mg three times daily regimen as soon as you say so. If you need to order a dose above the labeled maximum, that would need to go through pharmacy and your institution's override process, not through me."
